{
  "_comment": [
    "Provider-free reference book and expected-figure register (#266), the shared oracle for the #260 sub-audits.",
    "Steps are public /api/v1 requests, replayed in order by backend/internal/api/reference_book_test.go (seedReferenceBook) and e2e/playwright/support/reference-book.ts (seedReferenceBook).",
    "A string '@key' anywhere in a body, or a path segment '@key', is the id captured under that key. 'capture' maps a key to a dotted path in the response. Readers pre-bind '@EUR', '@USD' and '@system.<role>' for each system account. '{suffix}' in a string is replaced by the reader's run suffix (empty in Go; the browser database is shared within a run).",
    "A 'reconcile' step starts a statement session, selects every candidate dated on or before the statement date, and finishes it.",
    "Every register figure is derived by hand from the steps and the documented contracts (docs/implemented.md, docs/plans/budgets-plan.md, the ledger-invariants skill). Its 'why' is that derivation. No figure was produced by application code.",
    "A register mismatch is a finding: recheck the derivation, then file a defect. Never edit an expected value to match the app.",
    "Amounts are exact decimals compared by value, so '300' equals '300.0000'. Realized figures are signed as the API reports them: gain = proceeds + disposed basis, so a long's disposed basis is negative and a short's cover proceeds are negative. Dates are absolute and in the past so that dated reads are reproducible.",
    "A figure marked 'known_defect' names the open issue that makes the app disagree with it. Readers require it to still disagree, so the fix fails the reader until the marker is removed; the expected value itself is never changed."
  ],
